.TH SDL_HINT_VIDEO_X11_ENABLE_XSYNC_EXT 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_VIDEO_X11_ENABLE_XSYNC_EXT \- A variable controlling whether the X Synchronization Extension is enabled.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_X11_ENABLE_XSYNC_EXT \(dqSDL_VIDEO_X11_ENABLE_XSYNC_EXT\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If set, this can result in smoother window resizing when rendering using OpenGL, however, there are some conditions:
.PP

\(bu It is only activated on windows created with the
.BR SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL
flag (windows using an SDL OpenGL renderer have this automatically set)\[char46]
.PP
\(bu When activated, presentation must be done with
.BR SDL_GL_SwapWindow()

.BR "" ( SDL_RenderPresent()
calls this internally for OpenGL renderers as well)\[char46]
.PP
Enabling this and presenting via an external mechanism will result in sync requests not being acked, and hangs and other odd window behavior may result\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: The X Synchronization Extension is disabled\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: The X Synchronization Extension is enabled\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before creating a window\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]10\[char46]

